  "notes": "Modified cash basis (recorded as cash), same choices as FY2023. Governmental funds General, Street, CRA; business-type Water, Sewer. The governmental funds statement carries capital assets and depreciation, so the governmental roll-forward is on fund balance (p4-5): 2,066,818 + 697,094 - 369,604 + 75,000 - 75,000 = 2,394,308. Cash recorded separately where printed (p3: cash + county treasurer; CDs as investments; beginning from the 2021 Total column). Business-type: net position (Statement of Activities p2 / proprietary statement p7) 1,120,219 + 305,644 - 303,973 = 1,121,890; receipts total computed (operating revenues 303,288 + interest income 2,356). Water 'Returns' 5,037 is counted in Water charges for services on p2. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p3; totals equal the government-wide governmental column 2,394,308; fund balance by classification Assigned/Unassigned), business-type lines and totals from the Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: the only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary-basis budget-and-actual schedule (pp8-9), so detail is per-fund lines from the fund statements (p4, p7); budget schedule not recorded. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
